WEBVTT

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:18.220
Good. It's all done.

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:19.970
HAJIME HANAFUSA
UNI OF TEITO'S FIGHTER

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:22.350
Operation complete.

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:23.940
KOKOMI YOSHIZAWA
NURSE, UNI OF TEITO

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:24.940
I'm exhausted.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:30.190
-Doctor, how is he?
-Don't worry.

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:32.400
I've managed to bring him back.

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:34.450
MOKICHI ROBINSON, FIGHTER, SENTORY
(ELIMINATED)

00:00:34.530 --> 00:00:35.950
Your brother is going to be fine.

00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:37.870
ELENA ROBINSON
MOKICHI ROBINSON'S SISTER

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:38.830
Thank goodness.

00:00:39.410 --> 00:00:42.410
Thank you so much.
I can't thank you enough.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.920
You don't need to thank me.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:50.210
It was a rare opportunity for me to fiddle
around inside a living fighter's body.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:54.220
Doctor, don't say such a thing
in front of the family, please.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:58.640
Look!

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:01.100
Their match just finished.

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:05.980
<i>That guy...</i>

00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:42.070
FATHER AND SON

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:46.160
<i>In the Kengan Life-or-Death Tournament,</i>

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:48.250
<i>the fifth match of Block A</i>
<i>is about to begin.</i>

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:52.130
<i>The crowd is thrilled to be witnessing</i>
<i>the fight of the century</i>

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:54.340
<i>between two superhuman fighters.</i>

00:02:55.050 --> 00:02:57.960
<i>He's a decathlete known as</i>
<i>"The Immeasurable," Gozo Murobuchi.</i>

00:02:58.130 --> 00:02:59.590
GOZO MUROBUCHI
FIGHTER, UNITED CLOTHING

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:01.760
<i>His opponent is a championship contender,</i>

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:03.680
<i>Takeshi Wakatsuki,</i>
<i>also known as "Wild Tiger."</i>

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.390
TAKESHI WAKATSUKI
FIGHTER, FURUMI PHARMA

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:08.980
<i>Murobuchi is described</i>
<i>as a modern Hercules.</i>

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:12.900
<i>However, he has suffered</i>
<i>one previous defeat.</i>

00:03:13.310 --> 00:03:15.520
<i>And the man who defeated</i>
<i>him was Wakatsuki.</i>

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:20.400
<i>His challenge to</i>
<i>his long-standing foe begins now.</i>

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:33.580
We have a winner.

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:38.000
The winner is Takeshi Wakatsuki.

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:42.880
<i>That was... just incredible.</i>

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:45.050
OHMA TOKITA & KAZUO YAMASHITA
YAMASHITA CORP.

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:46.430
He hardly seems human.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:49.930
Ohma, do you think
you can you beat that guy?

00:03:50.020 --> 00:03:51.770
-I'm hungry.
-What?

00:03:52.190 --> 00:03:55.810
Wait. Are you sure you don't need
to watch the next match?

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:59.280
Nah. I don't care who I fight.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:04:02.950
Hey, Ohma.
You don't even have your wallet.

00:04:03.780 --> 00:04:06.870
<i>Excitement is only going to mount</i>
<i>as the sixth match will start soon!</i>

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:09.240
Oh, it's starting soon.

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:15.290
GAME SIX

00:04:15.380 --> 00:04:19.090
<i>This beautiful bird of darkness</i>
<i>dances bewitchingly.</i>

00:04:19.340 --> 00:04:21.420
<i>Don't let him get you under his spell.</i>

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:24.130
<i>This devil of a man</i>
<i>is now entering the arena!</i>

00:04:24.510 --> 00:04:28.010
<i>Standing 181 cm tall and weighing 74 kg,</i>

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:31.350
<i>his kengan match record is</i>
<i>four wins and no losses.</i>

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:33.390
SAYAKA KATAHARA
DAUGHTER OF METSUDO KATAHARA

00:04:33.520 --> 00:04:35.900
He has acquired total assets
of 21 billion, 90 million yen.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.610
Representing Murder Music,

00:04:38.860 --> 00:04:44.070
<i>also known as "The Bird of Darkness",</i>
<i>Keizaburo Sawada!</i>

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:53.960
It's finally my turn. I'm so excited.

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:55.540
KEIZABURO SAWADA
FIGHTER, MURDER MUSIC

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:59.290
And now, let's welcome the other fighter.

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:06.090
<i>This German muscle monster is</i>
<i>about to let loose in the Far East.</i>

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:10.850
<i>He has the biggest muscles</i>
<i>in human history.</i>

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:16.270
<i>No matter how powerful the attack,</i>
<i>it'll have little effect on this man.</i>

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:19.820
<i>Standing 205 cm tall and weighing 210 kg,</i>

00:05:19.900 --> 00:05:23.610
<i>his kengan match record is</i>
<i>51 wins and no losses.</i>

00:05:23.820 --> 00:05:29.490
He has amassed total assets of
1 trillion, 622 billion, 711 million yen.

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:31.620
Representing Toyo Electric Power Co,

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:36.460
<i>also known as "The Monster,"</i>
<i>Julius Reinhold!</i>

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:47.220
JULIUS REINHOLD
FIGHTER, TOYO ELECTRIC POWER CO

00:05:48.720 --> 00:05:50.720
You've got ugly muscles.

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:52.720
Not my type at all.

00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:54.680
We have a winner.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:55.980
We what?

00:05:56.060 --> 00:05:58.400
Due to Murder Music's default,

00:05:58.730 --> 00:06:04.280
Julius Reinhold of Toyo Electric Power Co
will advance to the second round.

00:06:04.650 --> 00:06:07.320
What the hell did you just say?

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:10.780
<i>That was unexpected.</i>

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:12.620
METSUDO KATAHARA
CHAIRMAN, KENGAN ASSOCIATION

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:14.200
ERIO KURE,
PATRIARCH OF THE KURE FAMILY

00:06:14.330 --> 00:06:17.120
Someone's finally taking advantage of
this tournament's idiosyncrasies.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:20.000
-Idiosyncrasies?
-Indeed.

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:25.090
This is a marathon tournament
spanning eight days in total.

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:28.800
There is plenty of time
to go on maneuvers.

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:31.260
Shall we penalize Toyo?

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:34.680
That's not necessary.
Let them do as they want.

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:40.690
I revised the rules to make it easier
for them to make deals under the table.

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:44.520
<i>Let them maneuver as much as they like.</i>

00:06:44.900 --> 00:06:46.480
YOSHIKO TOGAWA
PRESIDENT, MURDER MUSIC

00:06:46.650 --> 00:06:48.400
I'm sorry you had to go through this.

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:50.240
REN NIKAIDO
FIGHTER, BYAKUYA SHIMBUN COMPANY

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:52.570
Your brave decision has
ensured everything will go well.

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:58.830
<i>Goddamn it. I'm sorry, Sawada.</i>

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:02.830
Good job. We've got one position secured.

00:07:03.460 --> 00:07:06.000
Meguro, you're up next.

00:07:08.090 --> 00:07:09.670
MASAKI MEGURO
FIGHTER, UMIICHI SECURITIES

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:11.220
Time to break someone–-

00:07:12.970 --> 00:07:15.350
I knew this must be what was going on.

00:07:15.970 --> 00:07:17.890
You've gotta be kidding me, assholes.

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:20.310
You ganged up on a woman
and threatened her?

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:22.520
Do you even have balls? Huh?

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:25.520
What do you want, Keizaburo Sawada?

00:07:26.190 --> 00:07:29.190
Ms. Togawa chose to default
of her own free will.

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:32.990
-It's unjust to--
-Shut up, you Chinese jerk.

00:07:33.070 --> 00:07:36.740
Don't think you can get away with this
just because you're handsome.

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:39.620
I'm going to crush both of you.

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:41.000
Both of us?

00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:43.670
Don't you mean the three of us?

00:07:46.290 --> 00:07:47.460
<i>You've gotta be kidding me.</i>

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:51.130
<i>I kicked him so hard</i>
<i>his brain should be mush.</i>

00:07:52.090 --> 00:07:54.640
Yoshiko, stay out of the way.

00:07:54.760 --> 00:07:57.810
Sawada, fighting three fighters at once
is too much, even for you.

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:00.180
You know what?

00:08:03.520 --> 00:08:05.310
Men don't act out of reason.

00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:10.570
<i>Ballet requires more</i>
<i>flexibility than any sport.</i>

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:15.200
<i>If a ballet dancer</i>
<i>acquired kicking skills,</i>

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:16.910
<i>how mighty would they be?</i>

00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:22.160
<i>They would surpass</i>
<i>even a first-class martial artist.</i>

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:23.790
What?

00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:29.670
Hold on.

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:34.300
Keizaburo Sawada was
my opponent originally.

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:38.560
It makes sense for me to handle this.

00:08:39.890 --> 00:08:41.560
I don't need backup.

00:08:43.350 --> 00:08:46.730
Fine by me. You'll regret this.

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:48.060
Bring it on.

00:08:48.690 --> 00:08:49.730
Take this.

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:54.320
I'm putting extra G-force...

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:57.910
into this fatal attack.

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:03.580
<i>Sawada executed a successful kick</i>
<i>and destroyed Julius's cervical vertebrae.</i>

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:06.540
<i>Or so he thought.</i>

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:10.090
A kick aimed at cervical vertebrae...

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:13.300
Is that your technique?

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:19.470
Techniques, secrets...

00:09:19.970 --> 00:09:22.520
You fools are always
talking about those things.

00:09:23.060 --> 00:09:26.980
But it's just drivel for the weak,
it's nothing more than that.

00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:31.610
The truly strong don't need technique.

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:33.780
Sawada!

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:38.990
Just to be safe,
I'll break your left leg, too.

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:43.540
Darn. I missed.

00:09:45.910 --> 00:09:47.120
Another fool to take down?

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:51.420
Oh no! I didn't think
anybody would be there.

00:09:52.210 --> 00:09:54.420
I didn't see him
because he was in my blind spot.

00:09:55.010 --> 00:09:56.550
<i>They're Yamashita Corporation.</i>

00:09:57.590 --> 00:10:00.720
<i>It could be a problem</i>
<i>if something were to happen.</i>

00:10:01.850 --> 00:10:03.970
<i>I'll put him to sleep for a while.</i>

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:08.190
I'm terribly sorry.

00:10:08.520 --> 00:10:09.690
<i>What?</i>

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:14.530
<i>He predicted perfectly the trajectory</i>
<i>of a needle that's thinner than a hair.</i>

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:17.200
<i>Who is this man?</i>

00:10:17.450 --> 00:10:20.820
<i>Huh? I think I just saw something</i>
<i>whiz past.</i>

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:24.160
<i>-I have no choice.</i>
<i>-Nikaido.</i>

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:26.200
<i>That's enough.</i>

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:28.210
KATSUMASA HAYAMI
CHAIRMAN, TOYO ELECTRIC POWER CO

00:10:28.330 --> 00:10:29.920
Forget about Yamashita Corporation.

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:33.210
<i>Masaki, you should head to the arena.</i>

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:39.470
Your opponent is Muteba Gizenga.
He's a legendary mercenary.

00:10:40.180 --> 00:10:41.850
<i>Beat him to your heart's content.</i>

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:45.100
Got it, old man.

00:10:46.600 --> 00:10:49.520
You heard him. Let's drop it for now.

00:10:49.690 --> 00:10:51.310
There will be no next time.

00:10:52.230 --> 00:10:57.440
He... forgave me.
He's nicer than he looks.

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:03.280
Oh no! Are you all right?

00:11:05.830 --> 00:11:10.080
Let's raise a toast to celebrate
your victory in the first round.

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:11.880
To Ohma!

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:17.460
-You're not joining me?
-I'm starving.

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:21.050
Please let me do
what typical a president would do.

00:11:21.220 --> 00:11:25.010
I don't care about all that.
It's not a big deal, anyway.

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:29.480
It is. This is a huge step forward
for Yamashita Corporation.

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:34.190
Our company needs to pay off
the debt which I was forced into.

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:35.520
Whatever.

00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:41.320
Anyway, it was lucky
that Dr. Hanafusa came by.

00:11:41.910 --> 00:11:46.490
-I hope Mr. Sawada will get better soon.
-He'll be fine.

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:50.910
He looks shady but I hear
he's actually a very good doctor.

00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:55.040
Ohma.

00:11:55.670 --> 00:12:00.090
To tell you the truth,
I am very grateful to you.

00:12:01.930 --> 00:12:06.050
<i>All I used to do was flatter my boss,</i>
<i>but my life has changed completely.</i>

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:11.180
I've started to see the world
in a different way, as a man.

00:12:12.020 --> 00:12:14.690
What, Kazuo?
Do you want to fight, too?

00:12:14.770 --> 00:12:17.940
No. Combat sports are not for me.

00:12:18.110 --> 00:12:19.320
Says who?

00:12:20.650 --> 00:12:23.400
It's only about being strong or weak.
That's all.

00:12:25.990 --> 00:12:29.200
<i>News flash from the Kengan</i>
<i>Life-or-Death Tournament.</i>

00:12:29.330 --> 00:12:33.250
-We just saw that man.
-We happened to be on the scene, huh?

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:35.880
A surprise attack?

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:39.300
This tournament is getting intense.

00:12:39.380 --> 00:12:41.010
Who gives a shit?

00:12:41.550 --> 00:12:43.300
It's their fault for getting attacked.

00:12:43.420 --> 00:12:46.510
You know you could
get attacked too, Ohma.

00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:51.270
Even though you're incredibly strong,
I'm still worried.

00:12:51.640 --> 00:12:54.140
You have nothing to worry about, Kazuo.

00:12:54.270 --> 00:12:57.560
-You're wrong. You should listen to me.
-You're drunk, aren't you?

00:12:57.900 --> 00:13:02.690
Despite my appearance,
I'm old enough to be your father.

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:06.110
What's wrong with worrying
about my children?

00:13:06.700 --> 00:13:08.830
I don't give a shit
about a father or whatever.

00:13:10.910 --> 00:13:14.250
Besides, I'm not your son.

00:13:14.710 --> 00:13:17.170
That's true.

00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:25.010
Actually, I have a son,
though he never leaves his room.

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:28.930
I guess I have no right
to tell you what to do

00:13:29.430 --> 00:13:31.470
seeing as I'm not
a good father to my own son.

00:13:32.680 --> 00:13:35.520
-Where are you going, Ohma?
-To pee.

00:13:51.620 --> 00:13:53.240
<i>I'm Niko Tokita.</i>

00:13:54.250 --> 00:13:55.290
<i>Call me Niko.</i>

00:13:55.370 --> 00:13:57.170
NIKO TOKITA
OHMA'S MASTER OF NIKO STYLE

00:13:57.330 --> 00:13:59.630
<i>You don't have a name, do you?</i>

00:14:01.250 --> 00:14:04.760
<i>This area is between</i>
<i>Tokita and Shichi-ohma, right?</i>

00:14:05.090 --> 00:14:07.300
<i>Okay. "Ohma."</i>

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:10.890
<i>From now on, you're Ohma Tokita.</i>

00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:15.930
Don't act like my father.

00:14:16.520 --> 00:14:18.020
<i>Thank you for your patience.</i>

00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:20.520
It's time to introduce the next fighters.

00:14:22.770 --> 00:14:25.820
GAME SEVEN

00:14:25.900 --> 00:14:28.240
<i>Here comes the most</i>
<i>powerful creature in Africa,</i>

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:33.580
<i>the murder machine of the dark continent,</i>
<i>the ruthless mammonish warrior.</i>

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:37.710
<i>He has as many names</i>
<i>as there are legends about him.</i>

00:14:38.290 --> 00:14:43.130
<i>A legendary mercenary is now entering</i>
<i>the kengan match battlefield.</i>

00:14:43.710 --> 00:14:47.510
<i>Standing 199 cm tall and weighing 122 kg,</i>

00:14:47.800 --> 00:14:50.130
<i>this is his first kengan match appearance.</i>

00:14:50.760 --> 00:14:53.140
Representing Iwami Heavy Industries,

00:14:53.680 --> 00:14:59.190
<i>also known as "The Genocider,"</i>
<i>Muteba Gizenga!</i>

00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:07.490
MUTEBA GIZENGA
FIGHTER, IWAMI HEAVY INDUSTRIES

00:15:07.820 --> 00:15:09.650
TOMARI TOHGO
PRESIDENT, IWAMI HEAVY INDUSTRIES

00:15:09.780 --> 00:15:13.780
Show them, Muteba, that duty and
compassion mean nothing at all.

00:15:14.030 --> 00:15:17.450
And that it's the people who work
for money that are truly strong.

00:15:18.120 --> 00:15:21.420
Muteba Gizenga, the legendary mercenary.

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:25.130
Looks like Iwami Heavy Industries
dropped a bundle on this.

00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:28.340
That Iwami chick is wasting her efforts.

00:15:28.550 --> 00:15:31.380
<i>Next, let's introduce his opponent.</i>

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:38.770
<i>This man's background is unknown.</i>

00:15:39.230 --> 00:15:41.560
<i>His fighting style is unknown.</i>

00:15:41.850 --> 00:15:47.150
<i>This enigmatic monster is going to</i>
<i>run rampant in this kengan match.</i>

00:15:47.690 --> 00:15:51.280
<i>Standing 195 cm tall and weighing 130 kg,</i>

00:15:51.360 --> 00:15:54.370
<i>he makes his kengan match debut today.</i>

00:15:54.660 --> 00:15:56.910
Representing Umiichi Securities,

00:15:57.120 --> 00:16:03.170
<i>also known as "The Crying Man,"</i>
<i>Masaki Meguro!</i>

00:16:07.090 --> 00:16:08.920
I'm so excited.

00:16:09.300 --> 00:16:12.010
Should I break him?
Or should I strangle him?

00:16:12.340 --> 00:16:14.800
Or I could tear him apart.

00:16:17.970 --> 00:16:19.470
<i>He's crying blood!</i>

00:16:19.560 --> 00:16:24.020
<i>Meguro is entering the arena</i>
<i>with tears of blood running down his face!</i>

00:16:24.400 --> 00:16:26.520
<i>Watch me, Father.</i>

00:16:26.770 --> 00:16:31.490
<i>I'm going to kill him better</i>
<i>than the way I killed you.</i>

00:16:41.950 --> 00:16:44.620
-I made it.
-Where's Ohma?

00:16:44.710 --> 00:16:46.540
KAEDE AKIYAMA
NOGI GROUP CHAIRMAN'S SECRETARY

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:49.300
-He told me to not to wait for him.
-Okay.

00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:56.430
<i>That's the guy who attacked Mr. Sawada.</i>
<i>I had no idea he was a kengan fighter.</i>

00:16:56.720 --> 00:16:59.350
I'm going to kill him. Kill... Kill...

00:16:59.600 --> 00:17:03.180
Kill... Kill... Kill... Kill...

00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:10.070
You're breathing very heavily.
You're a psycho, aren't you?

00:17:10.650 --> 00:17:12.190
Take your stance.

00:17:13.240 --> 00:17:14.240
Fight!

00:17:17.450 --> 00:17:18.530
<i>That's judo.</i>

00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:19.740
Perfect.

00:17:20.740 --> 00:17:23.200
<i>M... Meguro got the mount.</i>

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:27.290
Play with him, Masaki.

00:17:28.500 --> 00:17:31.000
My father told me...

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:36.510
that judo is the strongest martial art.

00:17:37.260 --> 00:17:38.390
Cut the crap.

00:17:39.220 --> 00:17:43.390
<i>Muteba's trying hard to escape the mount.</i>

00:17:43.520 --> 00:17:47.350
<i>But it seems like his punches are less</i>
<i>effective because of his position.</i>

00:17:47.940 --> 00:17:50.940
Hey. Why aren't you wearing anything?

00:17:51.980 --> 00:17:54.860
I can't pull my usual move on you.

00:17:55.440 --> 00:17:58.570
<i>Meguro is strangling him!</i>

00:18:02.240 --> 00:18:03.240
You can't breathe?

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:06.370
Of course you can't.

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:10.040
If you see my father on the other side,

00:18:10.290 --> 00:18:14.170
tell him that I'm very grateful
to him for teaching me judo.

00:18:16.470 --> 00:18:18.130
Tell him yourself.

00:18:18.840 --> 00:18:20.640
<i>He smashed his eyeball!</i>

00:18:22.680 --> 00:18:24.930
<i>He barely flinched!</i>

00:18:26.140 --> 00:18:27.270
<i>In that case...</i>

00:18:30.440 --> 00:18:31.980
I'll only ask you once.

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:36.440
I was hired to win, not to kill.

00:18:37.070 --> 00:18:39.110
I'll let you choose.

00:18:39.490 --> 00:18:41.990
Will you surrender or die?

00:18:45.120 --> 00:18:47.330
<i>Did he just gain more power?</i>

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:52.500
<i>Impossible. Does he not feel pain?</i>

00:18:53.540 --> 00:18:55.000
<i>Damn freak.</i>

00:18:56.170 --> 00:18:59.840
<i>Wh... what is going on here?</i>

00:19:00.180 --> 00:19:03.600
<i>Meguro's suffered substantial injuries,</i>

00:19:03.720 --> 00:19:06.100
<i>yet is somehow able to</i>
<i>continue to attack Muteba!</i>

00:19:07.730 --> 00:19:10.850
I remember.
My father told me something else.

00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:13.150
His eye-for-an-eye policy was

00:19:14.110 --> 00:19:16.530
two eyes for one eye!

00:19:20.360 --> 00:19:23.240
<i>Meguro gouged his eyes out.</i>

00:19:23.660 --> 00:19:27.370
<i>Does this man not have a human heart?</i>

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:28.950
Here you go.

00:19:34.170 --> 00:19:37.090
<i>He got his testicles.</i>

00:19:37.300 --> 00:19:40.380
<i>That's Muteba's one brutal strike.</i>

00:19:43.470 --> 00:19:48.100
What are those people doing?
This is not combat sport.

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:50.140
I don't understand.

00:19:50.940 --> 00:19:53.770
Is he immortal?

00:19:54.810 --> 00:19:56.900
-Euphoria?
-Correct.

00:19:57.190 --> 00:20:00.570
It's one of the effects
of endogenous opiates,

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:02.950
such as endorphins and dopamine.

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:06.160
In other words, it's a pleasant sensation
produced by the brain.

00:20:06.620 --> 00:20:08.580
<i>Meguro has a unique constitution</i>

00:20:08.700 --> 00:20:12.420
<i>in which his brain secretes natural drugs</i>
<i>in proportion to the pain he feels.</i>

00:20:12.830 --> 00:20:17.420
<i>In short, any injury he receives</i>
<i>is converted into pleasure.</i>

00:20:18.210 --> 00:20:21.800
Although I have made some adjustments.

00:20:23.180 --> 00:20:27.100
<i>-He's smiling. Meguro is wearing a smile!</i>
-What's wrong? What's wrong?

00:20:27.430 --> 00:20:29.640
Are you okay, Father?

00:20:30.350 --> 00:20:32.440
Oh. You're suffering.

00:20:33.020 --> 00:20:35.690
Okay, then. Let me finish you off.

00:20:38.820 --> 00:20:40.190
Don't cry.

00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:42.530
That's no use.

00:20:42.610 --> 00:20:47.070
I can see you as well as if you were
sitting in the palm of my hand.

00:20:48.620 --> 00:20:50.040
<i>Muteba threw him away!</i>

00:20:50.370 --> 00:20:52.370
JERRY TYSON, FIGHTER, 22ND CENTURY FAX
(ELIMINATED)

00:20:52.500 --> 00:20:54.330
I don't understand
what's going on here at all.

00:20:54.620 --> 00:20:57.710
<i>Didn't Muteba lose his vision?</i>

00:20:57.790 --> 00:21:01.090
<i>How was he able to dodge Meguro's attacks</i>
<i>and deliver his blow?</i>

00:21:01.340 --> 00:21:05.180
The fighters have discovered his secret.

00:21:05.890 --> 00:21:10.640
<i>Muteba Gizenga,</i>
<i>he was blind from the start.</i>

00:21:11.810 --> 00:21:13.270
No way. That's impossible.

00:21:13.350 --> 00:21:17.810
He's been watching the matches
on the monitors.

00:21:18.020 --> 00:21:21.280
Are you dumb? He wasn't watching.

00:21:21.360 --> 00:21:26.160
<i>He was listening to the fighters'</i>
<i>movements through the monitor.</i>

00:21:27.200 --> 00:21:28.280
<i>Sounds.</i>

00:21:28.660 --> 00:21:30.660
<i>He uses echo location to detect terrain</i>

00:21:30.950 --> 00:21:34.660
<i>and predicts the moves his opponents</i>
<i>will make by picking up sounds.</i>

00:21:34.870 --> 00:21:36.290
<i>Smell.</i>

00:21:36.620 --> 00:21:39.920
<i>He determines the number of his enemies,</i>
<i>their physical health and equipment</i>

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:41.420
<i>based on smell.</i>

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:43.460
<i>Finally, touch.</i>

00:21:43.630 --> 00:21:47.550
<i>He fine-tunes the terrain information</i>
<i>he has already gathered.</i>

00:21:48.010 --> 00:21:53.680
<i>In his world, he can see better than</i>
<i>an ordinary man.</i>

00:21:55.100 --> 00:21:56.770
<i>How can you see?</i>

00:21:57.770 --> 00:22:02.820
You really are amazing... Father.

00:22:05.820 --> 00:22:07.910
<i>He's put his elbow back into its position.</i>

00:22:09.320 --> 00:22:11.240
Enough absurdity.

00:22:11.490 --> 00:22:14.700
Just die, you monster!

00:22:41.810 --> 00:22:44.650
You haven't trained your insides,
have you?

00:22:51.030 --> 00:22:53.030
<i>Masaki. Masaki.</i>

00:22:53.370 --> 00:22:54.410
"KEEP OUT! NO TRESPASSING"

00:22:54.490 --> 00:22:55.830
<i>Answer my question.</i>

00:22:56.200 --> 00:22:58.830
<i>Why did you have to kill</i>
<i>your senior disciples?</i>

00:23:01.080 --> 00:23:04.380
<i>Because I couldn't help it.</i>

00:23:06.420 --> 00:23:10.430
<i>I've been holding it in for 13 years.</i>

00:23:10.720 --> 00:23:13.850
<i>I couldn't hold myself back anymore.</i>

00:23:15.640 --> 00:23:20.640
<i>I realized my son was not human.</i>

00:23:21.940 --> 00:23:25.570
<i>He was just a monster</i>
<i>who'd been playing the role of a human...</i>

00:23:28.690 --> 00:23:30.820
<i>called Masaki Meguro.</i>

00:23:39.290 --> 00:23:41.460
<i>That was fun.</i>

00:23:44.130 --> 00:23:45.090
Meguro!

00:23:47.760 --> 00:23:53.340
We have a winner.
The winner is Muteba Gizenga.

00:23:57.310 --> 00:24:00.230
He was just a beast, after all.

00:24:00.680 --> 00:24:01.730
It's not important.

00:24:01.810 --> 00:24:04.060
We have one fighter...

00:24:04.230 --> 00:24:07.780
actually, no, we have two fighters
moving into the second round.

00:24:10.780 --> 00:24:12.490
<i>That was horrible.</i>

00:24:12.820 --> 00:24:15.990
He delivered the death blow
without hesitation.

00:24:16.700 --> 00:24:20.660
-Killing him was going too far.
-I don't think so.

00:24:21.830 --> 00:24:24.080
He died because he was weak.

00:24:25.170 --> 00:24:28.590
The weaker one dies. It's the natural
order of things, isn't it?

00:24:28.670 --> 00:24:31.720
That's not true, Ohma.

00:24:32.470 --> 00:24:35.390
Killing somebody is never a good thing.

00:24:35.720 --> 00:24:37.350
As a matter of interest,

00:24:37.430 --> 00:24:40.930
you haven't killed anyone, have you, Ohma?

00:24:43.890 --> 00:24:46.690
<i>There's no need for you to feel guilty.</i>

00:24:48.270 --> 00:24:51.440
<i>I lost because I was weaker than him.</i>

00:24:52.030 --> 00:24:53.700
<i>That's all.</i>

00:24:56.120 --> 00:24:57.200
<i>But Ohma...</i>

00:24:58.530 --> 00:25:00.540
<i>Don't come over...</i>

00:25:02.040 --> 00:25:03.870
<i>to this side.</i>

00:25:08.290 --> 00:25:10.500
You wouldn't understand.

00:25:12.420 --> 00:25:16.050
-Ohma?
-Sorry. I'm going to take a nap.

00:25:16.840 --> 00:25:20.260
I'm a little tired.

00:25:21.560 --> 00:25:22.770
Ohma.

00:25:27.150 --> 00:25:29.650
Ohma Tokita.

00:25:30.230 --> 00:25:31.650
Poor man.

00:25:32.610 --> 00:25:34.740
He doesn't have much time left.

00:27:06.290 --> 00:27:07.540
PREVIEW

00:27:07.620 --> 00:27:09.000
<i>Sumo or Pro-Wrestling?</i>

00:27:09.080 --> 00:27:13.500
<i>That's the philosophical question</i>
<i>engraved on men's life stories.</i>

00:27:13.670 --> 00:27:16.590
<i>Neither one of them will give an inch.</i>

00:27:16.840 --> 00:27:19.800
<i>What do you believe in?</i>
<i>Next episode: "Faith"</i>

00:27:19.880 --> 00:27:21.220
Subtitle translation by
Miki Miyaji
